estion/id #uuid "01083ad9-2ef8-55b5-a0c4-a85dc2bfe174" :question/math-academy-id "q-130283" :question/problem "Given that\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{13}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-130283/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130283"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130301/selection/f8291cb8855f3f343f6897c8e6df825f622606a6aaeb2e1e1b3ddea7849b5f81" :answer/id #uuid "45df6e68-95ff-5317-9e4b-eaa85adfa092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130301/selection/934c57093e9fa1d17bb2103670fa7201e62d200ca1b7f017a12ea332f6d03a13" :answer/id #uuid "aa8a35dc-2d20-5fb7-a7b6-cde09370b30f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130301/selection/04429f4ea15eb4af81d44cead2195a435aa8607effac07fc8f0664fde9195a2c" :answer/id #uuid "a50837e7-df0f-54e0-8ed6-5a9e744aea2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130301/selection/f700f6d0fa744555e6e4a0e522ff9a821a5df46db491fd1e8a380eb946bab54a" :answer/id #uuid "0a6a59a3-d13d-535a-8dc2-99fb6bb4220a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130301/selection/7cce9e1426a7314f51e94aafdfeabc3d22b1c77fd061d55ffc33565fe81229d0" :answer/id #uuid "ae21326b-7ba5-5d77-b882-066abbd80efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130301/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27706dba-0275-59c7-94b1-374ad6393762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130301/selection/f700f6d0fa744555e6e4a0e522ff9a821a5df46db491fd1e8a380eb946bab54a" :answer-field/choices ["q-130301/selection/f8291cb8855f3f343f6897c8e6df825f622606a6aaeb2e1e1b3ddea7849b5f81" "q-130301/selection/934c57093e9fa1d17bb2103670fa7201e62d200ca1b7f017a12ea332f6d03a13" "q-130301/selection/04429f4ea15eb4af81d44cead2195a435aa8607effac07fc8f0664fde9195a2c" "q-130301/selection/f700f6d0fa744555e6e4a0e522ff9a821a5df46db491fd1e8a380eb946bab54a" "q-130301/selection/7cce9e1426a7314f51e94aafdfeabc3d22b1c77fd061d55ffc33565fe81229d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130301" :question/id #uuid "2af516b7-e7fe-5e6e-8cca-463d0861c5fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-130301" :question/problem "Given \n$T=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]$,\n which of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{23}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-130301/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130301"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4693"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_2 := R_2 +(- 4) \\cdot R_1$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_2:=R_2 + (-4) R_1$ means that we need to add $-4$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nCarrying out this row operation, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4+(-4)(1) & 2+(-4)(2) & -1+(-4)(3) \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4694"] :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4695"] :question/problem "Which elementary row operation could transform the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has been changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nNow, applying the operation $R_2:=R_2+1 \\cdot R_1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4+1\\cdot (-4) & 1+1\\cdot (-2) & 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation could be done by the operation \n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+1\\cdot R_1\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+R_1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4696"] :question/problem "Given that\n$[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ which elementary row operation could make $a_{22}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "In the given matrix, we have $a_{22}=5$ and we want to perform an elementary row operation that makes $a_{22}=0.$\n\n- We *cannot* make $a_{22}=0$ by switching two rows, because there are no rows with $0$ as the second entry.\n\n- We *cannot* multiply the second row by $0,$ because we are only allowed to multiply rows by *nonzero* constants.\n\n- However, we *can* add a multiple of another row to the $2$nd row to make $a_{22}=0.$\n\nLooking at the first row, we see that $a_{12}=1.$ If we add $-5$ times this entry to $a_{22},$ we will get $a_{22}=0$ as desired. So, the elementary row operation that we need to use is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1.\n$$\n\nApplying this operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1+(-5)\\cdot 3 & 5+(-5)\\cdot 1 & 6+(-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -16 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the desired elemetary row operation is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1,\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 -5 R_1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
